<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
<Document>
  <name>Ranwell 1959 water-table sites — Route A provisional (Script 43 v1.0.1)</name>
  <description>Derived data: the 14 digitised sites of Ranwell (1959) Fig. 3 placed by Script 43's Route-A similarity (Penlon Lake anchor, 1/4 km scale bar, rotation assumed grid-north-up). Sites 2, 3 and 7 are not digitised and are absent. Positions are PROVISIONAL: drag each placemark onto the slack Ranwell drew, save, and the corrected KML becomes the new digitisation (D-140 Revisit-if). Yellow = Route-B flagged (|DEM − tabulated OD| &gt; 2 m). Source: outputs/43_ranwell/43_05_ranwell_sites.geojson (EPSG:27700), reprojected to WGS84 with pyproj.</description>
  <Style id="site"><IconStyle><scale>1.1</scale><color>ff00d7ff</color><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><scale>0.9</scale></LabelStyle></Style>
  <Style id="flagged"><IconStyle><scale>1.2</scale><color>ff00ffff</color><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><scale>0.9</scale></LabelStyle></Style>
  <Placemark>
    <name>R1</name>
    <description>Ranwell (1959) Fig. 3 water-table pipe site 1. Tabulated height 9.11 m OD; DEM at Route-A position 9.49 m (residual +0.38 m). Nearest modern dipwell ceh6 at 54 m. PROVISIONAL Route-A position (grid-north-up similarity from Penlon Lake + scale bar, label-position proxy) — drag to the correct slack. OSGB E 242598.8 N 364675.8.</description>
    <styleUrl>#site</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="site_no"><value>1</value></Data>
